{"id": "EUVD-2026-71496", "enisaUuid": "4b0aa437-551d-3a96-b825-36371e89c8c8", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ntipc: avoid busy looping in tipc_exit_net()\n\nBlamed commit introduced a busy-wait loop in tipc_exit_net()\nto wait for pending UDP bearer cleanup works to complete:\n\n       while (atomic_read(&tn->wq_count))\n               cond_resched();\n\nThis loop can busy-wait for a long time if cond_resched() is a NOP. This\ntypically happens if the netns exit is executed by a high priority task,\nor under kernels configured without preemption (CONFIG_PREEMPT_NONE). In\nsuch cases, it wastes CPU cycles and can lead to soft lockups.\n\nFix this by replacing the busy loop with wait_var_event(), allowing the\nthread to sleep properly until the work queue count reaches zero.\n\nAccordingly, update cleanup_bearer() to use atomic_dec_and_test() and\nwake_up_var() to wake up the waiter when the count drops to zero.\n\nThis uses the global wait queue hash table, avoiding the need to bloat\nstruct tipc_net with a wait_queue_head_t. The atomic_dec_and_test()\nprovides the necessary memory barrier to ensure the wakeup is not missed.", "datePublished": "2026-09-04T16:48:11", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:47:10", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/99b82c8452887408ea908fdfa5df33c4a5dfa88f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/110bb16d37bdba03213156c0df37e7119c190936", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7672973957e3e20780afe5937a9fec70b72bc060", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/522d1d950b9e3b68190a6de7534827c8dccedb73", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c1481c94e74c955e0448ddf46b8615a44d840c1e"], "aliases": ["GHSA-8w3x-69pj-572x", "CVE-2026-80866"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "02772ca2-d0a3-3182-9bbb-77e8d3e6721a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "08c1b478-3b94-3c06-a2c1-df72b1f48991", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.5"}, {"id": "0c2bf0d9-764c-3052-a7c3-eb39e3304267", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "24693abf-b249-3dee-b7df-92cdbb1541ed", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "5603826b-4d4f-3e85-9495-bd399ad45f03", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "65240df2-bbc9-3ee2-b3f8-e5dcde7ac9a9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "04c26faa51d1e2fe71cf13c45791f5174c37f986 <c1481c94e74c955e0448ddf46b8615a44d840c1e"}, {"id": "82c9a3f2-ba3f-3ce4-8e57-824ca441d751", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "04c26faa51d1e2fe71cf13c45791f5174c37f986 <7672973957e3e20780afe5937a9fec70b72bc060"}, {"id": "848d6542-48df-3c39-8af8-6a2a5795cc7b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "04c26faa51d1e2fe71cf13c45791f5174c37f986 <522d1d950b9e3b68190a6de7534827c8dccedb73"}, {"id": "9a821332-0782-30f1-a2a0-a735e0cd5343", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "04c26faa51d1e2fe71cf13c45791f5174c37f986 <99b82c8452887408ea908fdfa5df33c4a5dfa88f"}, {"id": "9acccaec-8005-3f9c-a69c-f74d872e7015", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d1f76dfadaf8f47ed1753f97dbcbd41c16215ffa"}, {"id": "a481d193-701c-3cc9-afb6-7d966496f035", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "a99eb5c6-a6d6-318c-9cf3-1ddd0fd8ddc4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.10.42 <5.11"}, {"id": "bac62a55-97fd-353a-af2b-008bf195ed9d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "04c26faa51d1e2fe71cf13c45791f5174c37f986 <110bb16d37bdba0321